  "description": "T1. English Oak\tFront Garden: Observations: Visual evidence of an Oak Processionary Moth (OPM) nest present in the tree. Raise canopy to clear the property roof by 3m. Raise canopy to statutory clearance heights: 5.5m over the main road, 2.5m over the footpath.\rRemove dead branches throughout the crown exceeding 2.5cm in diameter. Inspect the crown for any adverse conditions.\rT5. Rowan\tFront Garden: Reduce branches to clear the adjacent property elevation/roof by up to 2m. Remove dead branches throughout the crown area that are over 2.5cm in diameter,  and inspect the crown for any adverse conditions.\rT10. London Plane\tRear Garden: Selectively raise the canopy to a height of between 8m & 10m by lifting the secondary trailing branches only or to the point where historical pruning points have been made. Remove dead branches throughout the crown area that are over 2.5cm in diameter, and inspect the crown for any adverse conditions.\rT12. Japanese Maple\tRear Garden: Judiciously reduce back to clear Phormiums.\rT15. Holm Oak\tRear Garden/North Boundary: Remove dead branches throughout the crown area that are over 2.5cm in diameter, and inspect the crown for any adverse conditions. Selectively reduce crown spread on the south and west flanks by 1.5m, pruning \rthe longer stem sections back to suitable growth points to leave a natural, rounded appearance. \rT16. Norway Maple\tRear Garden/North Boundary: Poor form/dieback through the crown and contributing to boundary wall failure.  Dismantle in sections to ground level and treat stump with ecoplugs to prevent\rregrowth. Overall life expectancy is significantly compromised\rT17.\tNorway Maple\tRear Garden/North Boundary: Poor form/dieback through the crown and contributing to boundary wall failure. Dismantle in sections to ground level and grind out the stump. Overall life expectancy is significantly compromised",
